<title>AUSTRIA: Austria plans to to convert debt to euro from 1999.</title>
<headline>Austria plans to to convert debt to euro from 1999.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria will convert its outstanding schilling debts into euros at the beginning of 1999 if the new single European currency starts on time, the state financing agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Chief treasurer Helmut Eder told Reuters that all schilling denominated debt listed on the Vienna stock exchange would be converted on January 1, 1999. He estimated some 800 billion schillings would be involved.</p>
<p>Austria's move follows similar announcements by France and Belgium. Eder said Austria hoped to make its bond issues more attractive by converting to the euro. -- Vienna Newsroom, 43-1-53112-258</p>
